{
 "file": "torch_accelerators.mdx",
 "units": [
  {
   "id": 0,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 1924,
   "end": 1946,
   "text": "# PyTorch accelerators",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 1948,
   "end": 2036,
   "text": "LeRobot supports multiple hardware acceleration options for both training and inference.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2038,
   "end": 2060,
   "text": "These options include:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2062,
   "end": 2136,
   "text": "- **CPU**: CPU executes all computations, no dedicated accelerator is used",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2137,
   "end": 2184,
   "text": "- **CUDA**: acceleration with NVIDIA & AMD GPUs",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2185,
   "end": 2232,
   "text": "- **MPS**: acceleration with Apple Silicon GPUs",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2233,
   "end": 2296,
   "text": "- **XPU**: acceleration with Intel integrated and discrete GPUs",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2298,
   "end": 2316,
   "text": "## Getting Started",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2318,
   "end": 2399,
   "text": "To use particular accelerator, a suitable version of PyTorch should be installed.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2401,
   "end": 2664,
   "text": "For CPU, CUDA, and MPS backends follow instructions provided on [PyTorch installation page](⟦0⟧).\nFor XPU backend, follow instructions from [PyTorch documentation](⟦1⟧).",
   "tokens": [
    "https://pytorch.org/get-started/locally",
    "https://docs.pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/get_start_xpu.html"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2666,
   "end": 2696,
   "text": "### Verifying the installation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2698,
   "end": 2769,
   "text": "After installation, accelerator availability can be verified by running",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2881,
   "end": 2917,
   "text": "## How to run training or evaluation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2919,
   "end": 3079,
   "text": "To select the desired accelerator, use the ⟦0⟧ flag when running ⟦1⟧ or ⟦2⟧. For example, to use MPS on Apple Silicon, run:",
   "tokens": [
    "`--policy.device`",
    "`lerobot-train`",
    "`lerobot-eval`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3192,
   "end": 3332,
   "text": "However, in most cases, presence of an accelerator is detected automatically and ⟦0⟧ parameter can be omitted from CLI commands.",
   "tokens": [
    "`policy.device`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3334,
   "end": 3352,
   "text": "## Mixed precision",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3354,
   "end": 3458,
   "text": "Training precision is owned by ⟦0⟧, which accepts ⟦1⟧ (default) and ⟦2⟧:",
   "tokens": [
    "`--accelerator.mixed_precision`",
    "`no`",
    "`bf16`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3556,
   "end": 3604,
   "text": "⟦0⟧ requires an accelerator that supports it.",
   "tokens": [
    "`bf16`"
   ]
  }
 ]
}